Z||000003||rogergarrison||02-01-2001||08:03 PM||||thanks, ez enough then with just 5. Off to Radio Shack for a couple of DIN connectors.<P>i made new round faces on all my gages, so I want to keep them since they match the rest. I dont want the aftermarket look.||||reg||1
Z||000004||tgowens||02-01-2001||08:29 PM||||there are connectors on each end of of that harness....just unplug it from the gauge unit and the other end should be on a metal clip on the left hand side of the console support....(behind the radio) <p>[This message has been edited by tgowens (edited 02-01-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||rogergarrison||02-02-2001||01:48 AM||||how much slack is in the wires when you unclip it? Im thinking of moving the whole assembly to center console between radio and shifter.||||reg||1
Z||000006||tgowens||02-02-2001||02:24 AM||||the wiring "harness" runs from the bottom of the console support (about equal to the bottom of the radio) to the bottom of the auxilary guages.........the wiring harness is approximately 15" in length so I would think you would have plenty (if you intend to run the wires in a horizontal position to the area between the radio and the shifter as opposed to a vertical position up to the auxilary gauges) ||||reg||1
